00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:38.945
right

00:09:38.945 --> 00:09:40.980
We've heard of various

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:41.781
explanations

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:42.915
for why

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:45.284
this entire process happened

00:09:45.284 --> 00:09:46.619
the way it did.

00:09:46.619 --> 00:09:47.820
So we'll see whether

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.455
the Justice Department views

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:50.523
this case

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:52.858
to to be something that requires

00:09:52.858 --> 00:09:54.060
further investigation,

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.194
whether this will become

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:57.129
a full criminal investigation

00:09:57.129 --> 00:09:59.065
or whether they will resolve it

00:09:59.065 --> 00:09:59.932
the way they have,

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:01.834
which is by having a review done

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:04.403
by the Chicago U.S. attorney John Laws.

